    
        COMMANDS TO PUSH LOCAL CHANGES TO GITHUB
   
   1. git branch 
      git status   
        (First, confirm you are on the local branch)
   
   2. git checkout "Name_of_localbranch" (If you are not on the "remote_branch", switch to it)
   
   3. git add . (Add the files you want to push to the staging area)
            or
      git add "filename"
      
   4. git commit -m "Your descriptive commit message here" (Commit your staged changes with a descriptive mssg)
   
   5. git push origin "branchname" (Push changes to the remote repo branch on github). 